Subject: [PATCH] avfoundation: compressed audio opt-in; per-player recovery

Source: edde746/MPVKit b8b922ec74b84ac3a496e29e226a3a3e91491045
Authors: cxfksword / MPVKit contributors, Alex Kim, edde746.
Source headers/licenses retained. Adapted for locked MPVUI mpv base.
Inputs: libmpv 0003, 0005, 0006, 0015, 0019, 0020, 0021, 0022, 0023.

Keep audio-spdif opt-in, PCM latency/session behavior, and host's shared
audio session. Reject explicit/exclusive routes. AO event requests PCM
recovery in owning core only; no global failure latch. Combine software
volume/mute with separate ao-volume/ao-mute; clamp amplification to unity.

Validate full IEC periods; bound loader requests, ES storage, startup,
decoder stalls, and teardown. Reject stale epochs/future offsets. Retain
slow-source preroll grace. Publish locked native clock; freeze parked/paused
clocks, reject stale reset ticks, rearm underruns. Source EOF waits for actual
Apple playhead drain.
Keep ordinary PCM short-read/timeouts. Finite epochs drain/reopen per file;
EOF restart never reuses stale timeline. Restart demand traversal after
initial/async PCM retry to preserve outstanding consumer requests.

Delay metadata <=250ms after minimum preroll for fast finite EOF; otherwise
use INT32_MAX and recover before byte ceiling. Bounded raw parser may park
~98ms before end. Settle only <=100ms+sample tail for >=250ms after true EOF,
contiguous delivery, prior native progress, and automatic native pause.
Never extrapolate parked clock. Larger/no-progress stalls recover PCM.
Tail liveness does not prove audibility.

Prior validation: Build/Tests/NativeAudio/run.py extracts locked implementation.
ASan/UBSan cover parsing, pull/clock/EOF/window/transport, 70-minute offsets,
per-player fallback/volume, core pause/reset/drain, finite priming teardown,
gapless EOF/reuse, metadata prefill, byte ceiling, and EOF-tail eligibility,
settlement/reset. AVPlayer probes support ceiling/endpoint findings.
Physical-route fidelity, Atmos, sustained real-time runs: unvalidated.

